const specs=[["Hostname","NOVA-DC01.nova.corp"],["VM ID","101"],["Hypervisor","NOVA-PROX01"],["CPU","2 vCPU"],["RAM","4 GiB"],["Operating system","Windows Server 2025 Standard"],["IP address","10.10.20.10/24"],["Network","INFRA / VLAN 20"],["Gateway","10.10.20.1"],["DNS order","10.10.20.11, 10.10.20.10"],["Domain","nova.corp"],["Virtual disks","80G OS · 60G attached data disk"],["Firmware / machine","OVMF / q35"],["NIC / bridge","net0 / vmbr1"],["Roles","AD DS, DNS"],["Services","NTDS, DNS, Netlogon"],["Replication partner","NOVA-DC02"]];
---
<section class="section compact"><div class="container grid-main dc-profile"><article>
<section class="content-section"><h2>What is NOVA-DC01?</h2><p>NOVA-DC01 is a Windows server that helps Nova Corp manage its company accounts and computers. When an employee signs in, it helps verify their identity. It also helps computers find other company services using DNS.</p><p>It is one of two Domain Controllers in the <strong>nova.corp</strong> domain. <a href={base+"systems/nova-dc02/"}>NOVA-DC02</a> provides a second copy of the directory and can serve clients when DC01 is unavailable.</p></section>
<section class="content-section"><h2>Why does the company need it?</h2><h3>Problem</h3><p>Without a central directory, each computer would need its own employee accounts. Adding a new employee, changing permissions or disabling an old account would require changes on multiple computers.</p><h3>Solution</h3><p>Nova Corp created one company domain using Active Directory. IT creates an account once, organizes it into the appropriate department and assigns group membership. Domain-joined workstations can then authenticate the employee using the central directory.</p><figure class="dc-diagram"><div class="dc-node">👤 Employee signs in</div><div class="dc-arrow">↓ Finds a domain controller</div><div class="dc-node">🛡️ NOVA-DC01 verifies identity</div><div class="dc-arrow">↓ Requests authorized access</div><div class="dc-node">📁 Company resources check permissions</div><figcaption>Central authentication lets employees use a company account; individual resources still enforce permissions.</figcaption></figure></section>
<section class="content-section"><h2>Finding company services</h2><h3>Problem</h3><p>Employees should not need to remember the IP address of every server. A workstation also needs to know which server provides domain authentication.</p><h3>Solution</h3><p>DC01 hosts internal DNS. A request for NOVA-FILES01 resolves to 10.10.20.20, while service records help Windows find the appropriate domain services. <a href={base+"learn/dns/"}>Learn how DNS works →</a></p></section>
<section class="content-section"><h2>Keeping the company working when a server fails</h2><p>IT added DC02 so the directory does not depend on one Domain Controller. During the controlled outage of DC01, the workstation selected DC02, accessed SYSVOL and the authorized IT share, and obtained fresh Kerberos tickets. The servers were checked for replication convergence after DC01 returned.</p><Files01DocumentImages ids={["dc02-sysvol-available","dc01-recovery-gpupdate"]}/></section>
<section class="content-section"><h2>Inside this server</h2><div class="card-list">{inside.map(([name,description,route])=><a class="system-card" href={base+route}><h3>{name}</h3><p>{description}</p><span class="readmore">Explore →</span></a>)}</div></section>
<section class="content-section"><h2>How DC01 connects to Nova Corp</h2><figure class="dc-diagram"><div class="dc-node"><a href={base+"systems/nova-client/"}>💻 NOVA-CLIENT</a><small>Requests sign-in and DNS</small></div><div class="dc-arrow">↓ via <a href={base+"systems/nova-fw01/"}>NOVA-FW01</a> when crossing networks</div><div class="dc-pair"><div class="dc-node"><strong>🛡️ NOVA-DC01</strong><small>Directory and DNS</small></div><div class="dc-arrow">↔<small>Replication</small></div><div class="dc-node"><a href={base+"systems/nova-dc02/"}>🛡️ NOVA-DC02</a><small>Directory and DNS</small></div></div><div class="dc-arrow">↓ Identity and DNS support</div><div class="dc-node"><a href={base+"systems/nova-files01/"}>🗄️ NOVA-FILES01</a><small>Checks access to shared documents</small></div><figcaption><a href={base+"systems/nova-prox01/"}>NOVA-PROX01</a> hosts these virtual machines. The file server stores documents; the domain controllers support identity and name resolution.</figcaption></figure></section>
<section class="content-section"><h2>Related tests and incidents</h2><div class="card-list">{incidents.map(([title,description,slug])=><a class="system-card" href={base+"incidents/"+slug+"/"}><h3>{title}</h3><p>{description}</p><span class="readmore">Read investigation →</span></a>)}</div><h3>Other recorded validation</h3><p>Directory health, LDAP and Kerberos service discovery, SYSVOL and NETLOGON, and Active Directory Recycle Bin recovery were tested. DC01 has a daily System State backup at 23:00; a complete System State restoration has not been demonstrated.</p><details><summary>Show technical checks</summary><pre><code>dcdiag /test:Advertising /test:SysVolCheck /test:NetLogons<br/>repadmin /replsummary<br/>repadmin /showrepl NOVA-DC01<br/>Resolve-DnsName -Type SRV "_ldap._tcp.dc._msdcs.nova.corp"</code></pre></details></section>
<section class="content-section"><details><summary>Related to this server</summary><p><a href={base+"computers/nova-dc01/"}>AD computer object</a> · <a href={base+"directory/ous/domain-controllers/"}>Domain Controllers OU</a></p>{linksForSystem("nova-dc01").map(p=><p><a href={base+"policies/"+p.slug+"/"}>{p.name}</a></p>)}</details></section>
<section class="content-section"><h2>Engineering journals</h2>{[["CR-003 · Install Active Directory and DNS","Journal-CR-003"],["CR-004 · Additional domain controller","Journal-CR-004"],["CR-005 · Directory accounts and groups","Journal-CR-005"],["CR-013 · Directory resilience","CR-013_Secondary_Domain_Controller_and_AD_Resilience_Journal"]].map(([title,slug])=><p><a href={base+"reference/Documentation/Change-Requests/"+slug+"/"}>{title} →</a></p>)}<p><a href={base+"pdf-journals/Nova_Corp_CR-014_Engineering_Journal_and_Evidence.pdf"}>CR-014 · Controlled incident exercises →</a></p><p><a href={base+"reference/explore/systems/NOVA-DC01/"}>Original system reference →</a></p><p><a href={base+"reference/explore/virtualization/vms/101/"}>Exact VM configuration →</a></p></section>
</article><aside><div class="sidebox"><h3>Technical Profile</h3><dl class="fact-list">{specs.map(([label,value])=><div><dt>{label}</dt><dd>{value}</dd></div>)}</dl></div></aside></div></section>
<style>.dc-profile>*{min-width:0}.dc-profile .content-section{margin-bottom:45px}.dc-profile h2{font-size:clamp(1.65rem,2.6vw,2.35rem);line-height:1.2;margin:0 0 16px}.dc-profile p{line-height:1.7;margin:0 0 14px}.dc-profile h3{margin:20px 0 10px}.dc-profile pre{overflow:auto;max-width:100%}.dc-diagram{margin:20px 0;padding:20px;background:#1b201c;border:1px solid #586454;border-radius:10px;text-align:center}.dc-node{padding:14px;background:#282f28;border:1px solid #586454;border-radius:8px;display:grid;gap:6px;min-width:0;overflow-wrap:anywhere}.dc-node small,.dc-arrow small{display:block;color:#c5cebe;font-size:.8rem}.dc-pair{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) auto minmax(0,1fr);gap:10px;align-items:center}.dc-arrow{padding:12px 0;color:#e5d0ab;font-size:.8rem}.dc-diagram figcaption{font-size:.82rem;margin-top:16px;color:#c5cebe}.dc-profile aside{position:sticky;top:100px;max-height:calc(100vh - 120px);overflow:auto}@media(max-width:1000px){.dc-profile aside{position:static;max-height:none}}</style>
